# Deploy-script-generated marker + pre-deploy config snapshots on live hosts (.94/.19)
.deployed_commit
*.bak
!config.json
# BUGFIX (2026-08-29, live incident): config.yaml holds real deployment values
# (home subnet, gateway IP, safe_ips, etc.) that must stay real for the service to
# run, but was tracked in git -- meaning every commit either leaked the real network
# layout publicly, or (after a history-scrub) risked a `git reset --hard` silently
# overwriting the live file with anonymized placeholder values, which happened and
# briefly broke live subnet detection until caught. config.yaml.example is the
# tracked, safe-to-publish template instead; the real config.yaml is now
# deployment-local only, same as state/ and reports/ above.
config.yaml
# Same reasoning as config.yaml above, applied to v13: config_v13.example.yaml
# (dummy subnets/IPs) is the tracked template; a real config_v13.yaml on .19
# would hold this network's actual home_subnets and must never be committed.
config_v13.yaml
context/
# Environment Secrets
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

